WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.860
Two acids, at exactly the same
concentration: 25.0 milliliters of each.

2
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.660
Titrate each with the same alkali,

3
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.800
and both need exactly the same
volume to reach equivalence.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.480
Yet one of them is a strong
acid, and the other is weak.

5
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.660
So how can a titration
show which one is weak?

6
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.960
In this mission, you'll meet
the four shapes of pH curve,

7
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.900
for every pairing of strong
and weak acids and bases.

8
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.600
You'll find the intercept,

9
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.800
the equivalence point and the
half-equivalence point, and read off a pKa.

10
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: explain how a titration
curve reveals a weak acid.